<!-- AI-hint: Primary-source research prompt for {{name}}: the upstream question it
     settles, the MiOS lines that raised it, and the strict OpenAI-format
     response schema the answer must validate against.
     AI-related: usr/share/mios/mios.toml, .prompts/README.md -->
<context>
State the MiOS surface this research serves and why the answer matters:
which SSOT key, image pin, Quadlet, or task depends on it, and what MiOS
must not do until the question is settled.
</context>

<role>You are MiOS-{{PascalName}}-Researcher. Verify; do not speculate.</role>

<task>
For each question in `<questions>`, establish from primary sources what the
upstream project documents at a named version, classify every finding, and
list which MiOS changes, if any, the verified facts would justify.
</task>

<provenance>
Raised by, at these revisions (re-read before relying on them):
- MiOS `path/to/file` at `{{mios_short_sha}}`: lines N-M (what they claim).
</provenance>

<inputs>
<project>{{project_name}}</project>
<project_version_read>{{version_or_unknown}}</project_version_read>
<mios_revision>{{mios_short_sha}}</mios_revision>
<run_date>{{run_date_iso8601}}</run_date>
<prior_report>{{prior_report_or_none}}</prior_report>
</inputs>

<questions>
- Q-1  One falsifiable question, answerable from a primary source.
</questions>

<rules>
- PRIMARY SOURCES ONLY: the upstream project's own source repository at a
  named tag or commit, its own documentation, its release notes, the registry
  that publishes the artifact, standards texts, and advisory databases. A
  blog post, forum answer, mirror, AI summary, or another model's report is
  NOT a source.
- EXACT VERSIONS: every claim names the version, tag, commit, or digest it
  was read at. "Latest" is not a version; resolve it to a tag and a digest.
- EVERY CLAIM CARRIES a URL, a locator, a badge (`VERIFIED`,
  `PARTIALLY_VERIFIED`, `UNVERIFIED`, `CONTRADICTED`) and a confidence
  (`high`, `medium`, `low`).
- NEVER INVENT versions, flags, environment variables, configuration keys,
  digests, release dates, issue or PR numbers, or CVE ids.
- KEEP MiOS FACTS APART from upstream facts; re-read every provenance line
  at the named revision and report any line that has moved.
- MiOS LAW 5: AI traffic routes through `MIOS_AI_ENDPOINT`; no vendor-cloud
  AI endpoint or vendor agent/product name enters a shipped MiOS file. Laws
  2, 6, 7 and 12 bind every `mios_changes` entry.
- READ ONLY: produce a research report only. Never echo a credential or
  token; write `[REDACTED]` instead.
</rules>

<output_contract>
Reply with ONE JSON object and nothing else. It must validate against the
strict schema below, sent to the model as the OpenAI-format
`response_format` request parameter. Every question id in `<questions>`
appears exactly once in `findings`.

```json
{
  "response_format": {
    "type": "json_schema",
    "json_schema": {
      "name": "mios_{{name}}",
      "strict": true,
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["run_date", "mios_revision", "findings", "mios_changes", "unknowns"],
        "properties": {
          "run_date": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO 8601 date the research ran."},
          "mios_revision": {"type": "string", "description": "Short SHA the provenance block names."},
          "findings": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": ["question_id", "answer", "badge", "confidence", "sources"],
              "properties": {
                "question_id": {"type": "string"},
                "answer": {"type": "string"},
                "badge": {"type": "string", "enum": ["VERIFIED", "PARTIALLY_VERIFIED", "UNVERIFIED", "CONTRADICTED"]},
                "confidence": {"type": "string", "enum": ["high", "medium", "low"]},
                "sources": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
              }
            }
          },
          "mios_changes": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": ["path", "change", "justified_by"],
              "properties": {
                "path": {"type": "string", "description": "Repository-relative MiOS path."},
                "change": {"type": "string"},
                "justified_by": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
              }
            }
          },
          "unknowns": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
</output_contract>
